    <briefdescription>
<para>Svensson Fitting method. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Fits a discount function to the form <formula id="398">$ d(t) = \exp^{-r t}, $</formula> where the zero rate <formula id="399">$r$</formula> is defined as <formula id="401">\[ r \equiv c_0 + (c_0 + c_1)(\frac {1 - exp^{-\kappa t}}{\kappa t}) - c_2exp^{ - \kappa t} + c_3{(\frac{1 - exp^{-\kappa_1 t}}{\kappa_1 t} -exp^{-\kappa_1 t})}. \]</formula> See: Svensson, L. (1994). Estimating and interpreting forward interest rates: Sweden 1992-4. Discussion paper, Centre for Economic Policy Research(1051). </para>    </detaileddescription>
